   00001| #!/usr/bin/env node
   00002| // Apply the links notation rules of data/meta/notation-rules.lino by rule,
   00003| // one family at a time (PR #1188, R1188-U6; docs/links-notation-style.md).
   00004| //
   00005| // The rule: a name of the notation we own is spelled with `-`, not `_`.
   00006| // A family names its `.lino` files. Its names are the unquoted `_` names of
   00007| // those files that occur in no other `.lino` file (a shared name waits for the
   00008| // family that owns all its files), less the names a shell, Python or workflow
   00009| // file spells (the pass rewrites JavaScript and Rust only) and the names the
   00010| // family keeps with a reason. For each name the pass rewrites:
   00011| //
   00012| //   - the family's `.lino` files, and their byte mirrors (rust/embedded/,
   00013| //     and the untracked deploy copies js/seed/ and the engine package assets);
   00014| //   - the code that reads them: the name as a token inside a string literal
   00015| //     of js/, scripts/, rust/src/, rust/tests/ and the other reader roots, and
   00016| //     inside a JavaScript regular expression, where it accepts both spellings
   00017| //     during the transition (`specialization[-_]ceiling`); a comment mention
   00018| //     too, unless the same spelling is a code identifier somewhere, since code
   00019| //     identifiers follow their language's convention and are never touched;
   00020| //   - the backticked mentions in the documentation we own (not the case
   00021| //     studies and logs, which are history).
   00022| //
   00023| // Every renamed name is recorded in data/meta/notation-renames.lino, so the
   00024| // check can prove no reader went back to an old spelling.
   00025| //
   00026| // A family with `rule concise-lexemes` instead writes each long lexeme block
   00027| // that has one in the concise form (scripts/lib/notation-concise-lexemes.mjs),
   00028| // file by file, only when the result parses to the same tree; its check fails
   00029| // while a family file still holds a long lexeme with a concise form. ts/ is regenerated
   00030| // with `node scripts/translate-es.mjs --write` after a pass.
   00031| //
   00032| // Usage:
   00033| //   node experiments/formal_ai_subagent/apply-notation-rules.mjs --family <name> --write
   00034| //   node experiments/formal_ai_subagent/apply-notation-rules.mjs --family <name> --list
   00035| //   node experiments/formal_ai_subagent/apply-notation-rules.mjs --family <name> --files [--lines]   (what would change)
   00036| //   node experiments/formal_ai_subagent/apply-notation-rules.mjs --check
